============================================================
UNIFIED TRIPLE CORRESPONDENCE
============================================================

    ABSTRACT ROLE  |  FIXED (preserves)   |  BOUNDARY (breaks)      |  FREE (creates)
    ===============|======================|=========================|=====================
    Eisenstein     |  Inert (p≡2 mod 3)   |  Ramified (p=3)         |  Split (p≡1 mod 3)
    Computation    |  Lossless             |  Lossy                  |  Crystallization
    Metagraph      |  SC-SC (spine)        |  SC-NS (ribs)           |  NS-NS (sea)
    Tile pairs     |  Same-End             |  Cross-End              |  Disjoint
    Three Functors |  F1 (linear)          |  F2 (nonlinear local)   |  F3 (algebraic global)
    Triangle sides |  Hypotenuse           |  Vertical leg           |  Horizontal leg
    Colors         |  Blue (grid-sym)      |  Black (generic)        |  Red (transpose)
    Extremes       |  Transitive (H=1)     |  Intermediate           |  Regular (H=max)
    Tiling decomp  |  Overlap (inner)      |  Wiring (boundary)      |  Apex
    Constants      |  √2 (ratio)           |  π (area/curve)         |  e (growth)
    Primes         |  2                    |  3                      |  7
    ===============|======================|=========================|=====================

    KEY PROPERTIES:
    FIXED:    Exact formulas. Self-interaction. Diagonal. Small fraction. Stable under recursion.
    BOUNDARY: Bipartite. Interface. Always triangle-free. Carries frustration/curvature.
    FREE:     Statistical. Dominates at large n. Computationally irreducible. Generic.

    PRODUCT: 2 × 3 × 7 = 42 = the triple point where all three coexist.
    
  CONSISTENCY CHECKS:

  1. Spine is FIXED under complement Z₂ (SC classes = self-complement).
     Same-end is FIXED under vertex incidence (tiles share a vertex).
     F1 is FIXED under composition (linear = identity-like).
     → ALL 'FIXED' elements are stabilized by the relevant symmetry. ✓

  2. Ribs are BOUNDARY (bipartite, triangle-free) by THM-A.
     Cross-end is BOUNDARY — one tile's upper = other's lower (handoff).
     F2 is BOUNDARY — where nonlinearity first appears.
     → ALL 'BOUNDARY' elements are interfaces between two phases. ✓

  3. Sea dominates (96% at n=8).
     Disjoint pairs dominate (see dominance test).
     F3 is global (irreducible evaluation of independence polynomial).
     → ALL 'FREE' elements are generic/dominant. ✓

  4. FIXED carries exact formulas:
     Same-end: c = -2^{max(1,|s₁-s₂|-1)} (EXACT at all tested n)
     Cross-end: c = 2^{s₁+s₂-2} (EXACT)
     Disjoint: NO clean formula (ratio varies). → FREE = statistical. ✓
